<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani money market rates remain high.</title>
<headline>Pakistani money market rates remain high.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani money market rates remained high on Monday owing to a shortage of funds, dealers said. Overnight rates remained unchanged in the interbank market and deals were done at 17 percent, a dealer at KASB &amp; Co said. Term rates continued to ease off gradually due to an expected inflow of about 13 billion rupees between now and the end of this month, the dealer said.</p>
</text>
